---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site';
import { absoluteUrl } from '../data/tools';

const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: absoluteUrl('/') },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Privacy', item: absoluteUrl('/privacy/') },
    ],
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    name: 'Privacy Policy',
    description: `${siteConfig.name} privacy policy: calculators run in your browser; cookies, Google AdSense and GA4 disclosures, and how to opt out of personalized ads.`,
    url: absoluteUrl('/privacy/'),
    isPartOf: { '@id': `${absoluteUrl('/')}#website` },
    dateModified: siteConfig.contentUpdated,
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Cookies & Ads"
  description={`${siteConfig.name} privacy policy: calculators run in your browser; cookies, Google AdSense and GA4 disclosures, and how to opt out of personalized ads.`}
  canonicalPath="/privacy/"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Privacy' }]} />
  <article class="container prose panel" style="margin:1rem auto 3rem;max-width:800px">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="answer-first">
      {siteConfig.name} calculator inputs are processed in your browser and are not uploaded to our servers as part
      of the static site. This policy explains cookies, analytics, and advertising disclosures.
    </p>
    <p>Last updated 2026-11-13</p>
    <h2>Information we process</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Calculator inputs:</strong> stay on your device unless you voluntarily share a URL that
        contains query parameters.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Contact:</strong> if you email {siteConfig.contactEmail} or use the optional contact
        form (EmailJS when configured), we receive your message to respond. The form sends name,
        email, and message via EmailJS’s API; see their privacy policy. We do not sell contact data.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Logs:</strong> hosting providers may log standard request metadata (IP, user agent) for
        security and reliability.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Cookies, analytics, and advertising</h2>
    <p>
      We may use Google Analytics 4 to understand aggregate traffic. The GA4 library may load after
      interaction or idle time. Consent Mode v2 defaults keep <code>analytics_storage</code> and
      ad-related storage denied until consent is granted. Third-party vendors, including Google, may use
      cookies to serve ads based on a user’s prior visits to this or other websites when Google AdSense is
      enabled.
    </p>
    <h2>Which consent tool applies</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>EEA, United Kingdom, and Switzerland:</strong> when AdSense is enabled, Google’s certified
      consent message (Funding Choices / Privacy &amp; messaging, IAB TCF v2.2 via
      <code>adsbygoogle.js</code> and <code>fundingchoicesmessages.google.com</code>) collects consent for
      personalized ads and related purposes. The site’s own cookie bar is not shown in those regions so you
      only see Google’s message. Consent Mode stays denied for those regions until Google’s CMP records a
      choice.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Other regions:</strong> the site shows a small first-party cookie notice (Accept / Reject).
      Analytics and ad-storage Consent Mode signals stay denied until you Accept. Reject keeps them denied.
      Google’s European regulations CMP message is not used outside the EEA, UK, and Switzerland.
    </p>
    <p>
      Google’s use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads based on your visits to
      this site and/or other sites on the Internet. You may opt out of personalized advertising by visiting
      <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" rel="noopener">Ads Settings</a>. Alternatively, you can
      opt out of some third-party vendors’ use of cookies for personalized advertising by visiting
      <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="noopener">www.aboutads.info</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Learn more about how Google uses data:
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener"
        >How Google uses information from sites or apps that use our services</a
      >.
    </p>
    <h2>DoubleClick / personalized ads</h2>
    <p>
      When AdSense is active, Google may use the DoubleClick cookie for ad serving and measurement. Use the
      opt-out links above to manage personalized ads. In the EEA, UK, and Switzerland, personalized ads
      depend on the Google-certified CMP described above (IAB TCF v2.2).
    </p>
    <h2>Data retention</h2>
    <p>
      Calculator inputs are not stored on {siteConfig.name} servers. Contact emails are kept only as long as needed
      to respond and maintain the public correction log when a fix is documented. Hosting access logs follow
      the retention policy of the hosting provider and are used for security and reliability, not for
      building marketing profiles.
    </p>
    <h2>Children’s privacy</h2>
    <p>
      The site is a general-audience planning tool and is not directed at children under 13. We do not
      knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has sent us personal
      information, contact {siteConfig.contactEmail} and we will delete it.
    </p>
    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      When this policy changes, the “Last updated” date at the top of the page will change. Material changes
      to advertising or analytics practices will be described here before personalized ads are enabled.
    </p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Privacy questions: <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`}>{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a> or the
      <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
